# Post-mortem: small-jam (seed 1)

**Generated by** switchyard-analysis 0.1.0 · 8 replays (8 changes × 1 history) · loss scored at 00:37 (window end + 10 min) · **noise band** ± 42 parcel-min [R0]

## Summary

From 00:11 sorted throughput fell up to 62 % below the fault-free twin. By 00:37 the incident had cost **837 parcel-minutes** of delay, and 23 parcels were more than 10 min late [R0].
Chute C0 jams (F0) explains 99 % (827 parcel-min) [R1]; robot R7 breaks down (F1) explains 1 % (10 parcel-min) [R2]. 0 parcel-min (0 %) is not explained by removing these causes [R3].

Best fix: **send chute C0's destination to C1 while it is jammed** would have recovered 595 parcel-min (71 % of the loss) [X2].

