| 1 | chute C0 jams (F0) | 827 ± 42 | 99 % | 832 | 822 | 1 | [R1, R2] |
| 2 | robot R7 breaks down (F1) | 10 ± 42 | 1 % | 15 | 5 | 0 | [R2, R1] |

Interactions: none beyond the noise; the causes add up independently.

Smallest set of causes whose removal recovers at least 90 % of the recoverable loss: {F0} [R1].

## Trigger and detection

Trigger: chute C0 jams at 00:10 (F0) [A].
Detection: a one-sided CUSUM on the per-minute shortfall against the twin (k = 0.5, h = 3 in units of the twin's Poisson noise) alarmed at 00:19; the incident window runs 00:11 to 00:27 [A, T].

## Resolution

Throughput was back within 5 % of the twin, and held there, 14 min after the window opened [A, T].

